{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2's dedicated uploader identity with an SSH key accepted by a separate ingest application identity on node1, without replacing administrative access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has a password-locked uploader account and dedicated 2048-bit RSA key. Node1 has a distinct password-locked ingest account whose matching authorized key is root-controlled and restricted to node2's address. Administrative access as antrieb continued independently.","evidence_ids":["cmd-202ba87c127d4e56","cmd-3e59407aaa7c411e","cmd-edb3913813d84e05","cmd-c84fd5fa18294076"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Accept newline-delimited submissions from node2 and store each completed submission as a separate file under /srv/legacy2/ssh-forced-command-ingest/received on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A two-line batch was submitted through the uploader key and stored as a separate 0600 receipt with an identical checksum. Additional submissions produced distinct receipt files, including successful end-to-end submissions after each restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89f1266d90874ee1","cmd-e03859512bfb47a7","cmd-c826cc5a60e24310","cmd-8b89b918c9464c9e","cmd-c84fd5fa18294076"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent this SSH identity from executing arbitrary commands, obtaining a shell or PTY, or establishing forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote-command and PTY attempts returned 126, command-like stdin was stored literally without execution, escape-marker files remained absent, and live forwarding attempts were rejected as administratively prohibited. These restrictions were directly retested after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-36da87f7ca314cfc","cmd-e5b3750ad0a0441f","cmd-f868f5eaec664f8f","cmd-16753be46bbc4478","cmd-eb7dc5b40be84722"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the existing receipt and sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original sample-batch.txt and received/prior.txt retained their initial contents, sizes, and MD5 checksums through the final state, while new receipts were added separately.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-91c81fff6553460f","cmd-e03859512bfb47a7","cmd-c84fd5fa18294076"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 before and after execution. The implementation used the installed OpenSSH 4.3-era facilities and POSIX shell tools, and it functioned after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9cf399b4e209460d","cmd-ae0bb903bc624e6a","cmd-8b89b918c9464c9e","cmd-c84fd5fa18294076","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"No unrelated configuration, package, service, or security mutation was evident; failed early submission attempts either made no demonstrated state change or created prerequisites used by the final solution. Cleanup was nevertheless incomplete: cmd-e5b3750ad0a0441f left /tmp/ingest-forward.log and its PID file, cmd-16753be46bbc4478 left the corresponding final-test log and PID file, and cmd-b939c2df829943a9 plus cmd-563829159ff54329 left reboot log files. All six low-risk artifacts remained in the after-executor snapshots. The forwarding processes themselves were stopped and no stale listener remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5b3750ad0a0441f","cmd-b939c2df829943a9","cmd-563829159ff54329","cmd-16753be46bbc4478","cmd-47437a05dd2b4a54","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered SSH, configuration, key/data, and end-to-end ingestion state.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshots were empty even though executor probes directly showed sshd listening, so those supplemental socket inventories do not independently corroborate service health.","Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy platform, and the lifecycle yum package-health probe invoked an unsupported command form; broad failed-service and package-consistency status therefore remain unassessed.","Temporary evidence and reboot log files were not removed after verification."]}
